    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1009">

                <pb facs="0882" n="766" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg766"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/3389.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the American
                        Ambassador</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.—Paraphrases.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-28T14:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 28, 1912—2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Regarding censorship, as per your March 26, 9 p.m. Protest vigorously if
                    necessary against refusal to receive consular or other official telegrams for
                    Embassy or Department.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
